  "title": "Unlike-Denominator Fraction Word Problems",
  "intro": "Teach common denominators as a way to work with equal-sized pieces.",
  "html": "<h2>Teaching notes for parents and teachers</h2><h3>How to teach it</h3><p>Keep one foot as the reference whole and draw both fractions on matching strips. Rename them before combining or subtracting.</p><h3>Example to work through together</h3><p>Use the model below as you explain the example. Have your student point to the quantities as you discuss them.</p><div class=\"model unlike-fraction-model\"><p class=\"sample-equation\">1/2 + 1/3 = 3/6 + 2/6 = 5/6 foot</p><svg viewBox=\"0 0 370 226\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three equal-length one-foot bars divided into sixths: three shaded sixths for one half, two for one third, and five for the sum.\" style=\"max-width:480px;width:100%;height:auto\"><text x=\"10\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">1/2 = 3/6</text><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"110\" y=\"7\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#217668\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"150\" y=\"7\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#217668\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"190\" y=\"7\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#217668\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"230\" y=\"7\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"270\" y=\"7\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"310\" y=\"7\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">1/3 = 2/6</text><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"110\" y=\"77\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#217668\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"150\" y=\"77\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#217668\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"190\" y=\"77\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"230\" y=\"77\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"270\" y=\"77\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"310\" y=\"77\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Sum: 5/6</text><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"110\" y=\"147\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#217668\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"150\" y=\"147\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#217668\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"190\" y=\"147\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#217668\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"230\" y=\"147\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#217668\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"270\" y=\"147\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#217668\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><rect class=\"sixth-cell\" x=\"310\" y=\"147\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#154d56\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"217\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"currentColor\">Each full bar represents 1 foot.</text></svg><p>The bars use the same whole and the same-sized sixths. Splitting one half into three sixths, or one third into two sixths, changes the way the length is named, not the amount of cable.</p></div><div class=\"model recipe-addition-model\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Fourteen twelfths of a cup\" style=\"overflow-x:auto\"><svg role=\"img\" aria-label=\"One cup and two twelfths of another cup: eight twelfths plus six twelfths\" viewBox=\"0 0 620 150\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;min-width:620px\"><title>Both cup bars use twelve equal parts</title><text x=\"10\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#164f5b\">Cup 1</text><rect class=\"initial-cup-part\" x=\"96\" y=\"15\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"initial-cup-part\" x=\"138\" y=\"15\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"initial-cup-part\" x=\"180\" y=\"15\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"initial-cup-part\" x=\"222\" y=\"15\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"initial-cup-part\" x=\"264\" y=\"15\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"initial-cup-part\" x=\"306\" y=\"15\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"initial-cup-part\" x=\"348\" y=\"15\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"initial-cup-part\" x=\"390\" y=\"15\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"added-cup-part\" x=\"432\" y=\"15\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#b74724\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"added-cup-part\" x=\"474\" y=\"15\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#b74724\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"added-cup-part\" x=\"516\" y=\"15\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#b74724\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"added-cup-part\" x=\"558\" y=\"15\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#b74724\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"107\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#164f5b\">Cup 2</text><rect class=\"added-cup-part\" x=\"96\" y=\"80\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#b74724\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"added-cup-part\" x=\"138\" y=\"80\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#b74724\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"empty-cup-part\" x=\"180\" y=\"80\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"empty-cup-part\" x=\"222\" y=\"80\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"empty-cup-part\" x=\"264\" y=\"80\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"empty-cup-part\" x=\"306\" y=\"80\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"empty-cup-part\" x=\"348\" y=\"80\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"empty-cup-part\" x=\"390\" y=\"80\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"empty-cup-part\" x=\"432\" y=\"80\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"empty-cup-part\" x=\"474\" y=\"80\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"empty-cup-part\" x=\"516\" y=\"80\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"empty-cup-part\" x=\"558\" y=\"80\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/></svg><p>Green shows the original 8/12 cup. Orange shows the added 6/12 cup. Each full bar is one cup, so the fourteen colored parts fill one whole cup and two twelfths of the next.</p></div><h3>Ask your student</h3><blockquote><p>How can we make the pieces the same size without changing either length?</p></blockquote><h3>If your student needs help</h3><p>If only the denominator changes, count how many new pieces replace each original piece.</p>",
